    {
      "id": "hi",
      "chapter": {
        "n": 1,
        "title": "Why"
      },
      "step": "Why",
      "lower": {
        "name": "Joaquin",
        "role": "Variantly"
      },
      "text": "This is Variantly. In the next ten minutes, I'll show you one whole run, including what it costs and how to undo it. I'm Joaquin, and I built Variantly because redesigning a site usually means betting on one direction. If it's wrong, you start over. Here, your agent builds several complete redesigns at once, each one running as your real site, and you keep the one you like.",
      "actions": [
        {
          "goto": "{{site}}"
        },
        {
          "wait": 3000
        },
        {
          "scroll": 900,
          "ms": 3200
        },
        {
          "wait": 2500
        },
        {
          "scroll": 2000,
          "ms": 3000
        },
        {
          "wait": 2000
        },
        {
          "scroll": 0,
          "ms": 2500
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "learn",
      "step": "Why",
      "card": {
        "kind": "learn",
        "title": "In this video",
        "items": [
          {
            "text": "Set up a run",
            "on": "setting"
          },
          {
            "text": "Give each variant its own direction",
            "on": "direction,"
          },
          {
            "text": "Compare them on your real site",
            "on": "comparing"
          },
          {
            "text": "Keep one, for the whole site",
            "on": "keeping"
          }
        ]
      },
      "text": "Here's what we'll cover: setting up a run, giving each variant its own direction, comparing them on your real site, and keeping one.",
      "actions": [
        {
          "wait": 300
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "model",
      "step": "Why",
      "diagram": {
        "kind": "flow",
        "title": "How it works",
        "nodes": [
          {
            "label": "Your repo",
            "sub": "untouched",
            "on": "project"
          },
          {
            "label": "Copies",
            "sub": "git worktrees",
            "on": "copy,"
          },
          {
            "label": "Previews",
            "sub": "own dev server",
            "on": "preview."
          },
          {
            "label": "Compare",
            "sub": "side by side",
            "on": "compare"
          },
          {
            "label": "Keep",
            "sub": "into your tree",
            "on": "keep,"
          },
          {
            "label": "Rollout",
            "sub": "every page",
            "on": "rolls"
          }
        ]
      },
      "text": "First, the mental model. Your project stays where it is. Each variant is its own copy: a git worktree on its own branch, a little timeline of your site, with a preview. You compare them side by side, keep one, and a last pass rolls it out to the whole site.",
      "actions": [
        {
          "wait": 300
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "need",
